{"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkCutTree"}],"externalID":"s:17LinkCutTreeModule0abC0V","remoteSource":{"fileName":"LinkCutTree.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/LinkCutTreeModule\/LinkCutTree.swift#L16"},"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"LinkCutTreeModule"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkCutTree"}],"title":"LinkCutTree","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct"},"abstract":[{"text":"A forest of rooted trees on the vertices ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that can be linked and cut, with a cost on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each vertex, and minimum, addition and subtraction along the path from a vertex to its root.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkCutTreeModule\/documentation\/LinkCutTreeModule"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkCutTreeModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/LinkCutTreeModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkCutTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cost","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cost","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdditiveArithmetic","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cost","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The dynamic trees of Sleator and Tarjan, as link–cut trees: the forest is split into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"preferred paths, each held in a splay tree ordered by depth, and the paths are joined by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"path-parent pointers. Every operation is O(log count) amortized.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A vertex’s cost belongs to the vertex, not to the edge to its parent, so path operations from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cover "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and its root and every vertex between them. To give edges costs, as Dinic’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithm with dynamic trees does, keep each edge’s cost at its child and a cost at each root"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that no path minimum should report."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every operation is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mutating"},{"type":"text","text":", queries included, because each one restructures the splay trees."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Storage is one array of nodes, copied on write."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/linkcuttreemodule\/linkcuttree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkCutTreeModule\/documentation\/LinkCutTreeModule\/LinkCutTree\/init(count:cost:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkCutTreeModule\/documentation\/LinkCutTreeModule\/LinkCutTree\/count"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkCutTreeModule\/doc